From 163070f743474493fd376175d5b80010536b5ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:59:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Trim Cloud VPS copy (provider list, UpCloud connect,
 backup/reimage warnings)

Fourth pass on the "too many words" feedback -- Cloud VPS (UpCloud/Azure/
Hetzner). Same approach as Panel: the data-dense screens (server detail,
create-success, create-confirm) are left alone, since their length comes
from actual fields, not prose. Trimmed the ones that had restatement:
  - cloud_provider_list: dropped the "buy and manage via cloud-provider
    APIs" subtitle, kept just the call to action.
  - cloud_step_username_upcloud: cut down to the one clarifying detail
    (same login as upcloud.com) without the surrounding sentence.
  - cloud_backup_restore_confirm, azure_vm_reimage_confirm: kept the
    actual warnings (data replaced/wiped, server must be off) but as
    plain short sentences instead of two clauses each.
  - azure_create_waiting_username: same username-rules constraint, fewer
    words spent introducing it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NFMuHFMb7r1xEwqxGw4pZn
